    "answer": "The prediction API is experiencing issues because the deployment `prediction-api` in namespace `mlops-app` was updated to a container image that does not exist (`mlops-inference:9.9.9-missing`), causing new pods to fail to pull the image and remain in an `ImagePullBackOff` state.\n\n---\n\n**Known facts**\n- Service `prediction-api` has 1 ready endpoint and 2 not-ready endpoints `[E-35e83d]`, `[E-39324d]`.\n- Deployment `prediction-api` requests 2 desired replicas, but only 1 replica is currently ready and available `[E-48ad43]`, `[E-8cd83b]`.\n- The deployment is configured with image `mlops-inference:9.9.9-missing` `[E-48ad43]`, `[E-8cd83b]`.\n- Two new pods (`prediction-api-7776c46b7-srxdq` and `prediction-api-7776c46b7-vs8sg`) are stuck in `Pending` phase with state `ImagePullBackOff` / `ErrImagePull` `[E-21b8d9]`, `[E-e8b6f0]`, `[E-39324d]`.\n- Kubernetes events show image pull failures stating: `Failed to pull image \"mlops-inference:9.9.9-missing\": repository does not exist or may require authorization` `[E-21b8d9]`, `[E-50b95c]`, `[E-39324d]`.\n- One pod from a previous ReplicaSet (`prediction-api-66888ff654-kpwvk`) running image `docker.io/library/mlops-inference:1.0.0` remains `Running` and ready `[E-e8b6f0]`, `[E-39324d]`.\n- ConfigMap settings associated with the deployment specify `APP_VERSION`: `1.0.0`, `MODEL_VERSION`: `1`, and `MODEL_PATH`: `/app/serving/model/model.joblib` `[E-8cd83b]`.\n\n**Uncertainties**\n- Who or what initiated the deployment update to tag `9.9.9-missing`.\n- Whether a valid `mlops-inference:1.0.0` or other valid container image tag should be restored in the deployment specification.\n\n**Recommended actions**\n1. Update the deployment `prediction-api` container image specification from `mlops-inference:9.9.9-missing` back to a valid tag (such as `mlops-inference:1.0.0`).\n2. After updating the deployment image tag, request a rolling restart of deployment `prediction-api` in namespace `mlops-app` (requires user confirmation before execution).",
